[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 build for the [B]Huawei Y220-U05[/B]. It is made for the MediaTek MT6572 NAND layout used by stock firmware C482B206SP05. System, data and cache are UBIFS volumes; this is not an eMMC device and it is not the Huawei Y210.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only flash this on Huawei Y220-U05. This device does not provide standard fastboot.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status — Stable[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]recovery-twrp-3.1.1-0.1-y220-u05-20261021.img[/B]

Tested on real hardware with kernel #92:

[LIST]
[*]Boot to recovery, touchscreen and 320x480 display
[*]Capacitive Back and Home keys
[*]ADB in recovery, reported as [B]Y220-U05[/B]
[*]Mount /system, /data and /cache (UBIFS) and the external microSD
[*][B]Backup[/B] of system, data, cache, boot and recovery to the microSD, from the GUI and from the command line, with valid MD5 files
[*][B]Restore[/B] of system, data, cache and boot in a single run (191 MB in 48 s), followed by a normal Android boot
[*]Wipe cache, Dalvik cache and factory reset
[*][B]Install ZIP[/B] from the microSD ([URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/rom-unofficial-2-3-7-cyanogenmod-7-for-huawei-y220-u05.4805983/"]CyanogenMod 7[/URL], [URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/rom-unofficial-4-2-2-cyanogenmod-10-1-for-huawei-y220-u05.4806135/"]CyanogenMod 10.1[/URL] and the stock ROM ZIP)
[*]TWRP settings stored on the external microSD
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Important NAND / UBIFS notes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]The recovery partition is NAND MTD8 and is exactly 6 MiB (6291456 bytes).
[*]Backups of system, data and cache are file-based UBIFS archives; boot and recovery are raw MTD images.
[*]Keep backups on the external microSD. The phone has no emulated internal storage, and /data is too small.
[*]Do not flash an ext4 or YAFFS system image to MTD14. Install compatible ROM ZIPs through TWRP.
[*]Never use [B]Format All[/B] in SP Flash Tool. It can erase NVRAM, IMEI and calibration data.
[*]If SP Flash Tool is required, use a compatible [B]v5[/B] release and select only the recovery partition.
[*]Tip: in [B]Settings[/B], enable the digest (MD5) verification of backup files, so TWRP checks a backup before restoring it.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Before starting:[/B] back up NVRAM/pro_info/protect partitions and copy the backup away from the phone.

[B]Method 1 — updating from an older TWRP on the phone:[/B]

Copy the image to the microSD, boot to TWRP and run:

[CODE]adb shell
flash_image recovery /external_sd/recovery-twrp-3.1.1-0.1-y220-u05-20261021.img
dd if=/dev/mtd/mtd8 bs=2048 count=3072 | md5sum
reboot recovery[/CODE]

The md5sum must match the one below before you reboot.

[B]Method 2 — from an already rooted system with a working flash_image:[/B]

[CODE]adb push recovery-twrp-3.1.1-0.1-y220-u05-20261021.img /data/local/tmp/recovery.img
adb shell
su
flash_image recovery /data/local/tmp/recovery.img
sync
reboot recovery[/CODE]

[B]Method 3 — SP Flash Tool v5:[/B]

[LIST=1]
[*]Load the correct scatter file for your exact Y220-U05 firmware.
[*]Choose [B]Download Only[/B].
[*]Uncheck every partition except [B]RECOVERY[/B].
[*]Select the downloaded recovery image for RECOVERY.
[*]Flash it, then boot directly to recovery.
[/LIST]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Do not select Format All and do not flash preloader, boot or NVRAM from another phone.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Entering recovery[/B][/SIZE]

From Android:

[CODE]adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

You can also use the hardware recovery key combination while the phone is powered off.

